// The Go workspace file.
//
// WHY IT EXISTS
// -------------
// This repository holds BOTH the legacy Laravel application and the Go
// rewrite, and the Laravel application's Composer dependencies live in
// `vendor/` at the repository ROOT.
//
// The Go toolchain sees a `vendor/` directory in the main module and
// concludes that it is a GO vendor directory — the one that `go mod vendor`
// writes, with a `modules.txt` manifest and all. Composer writes none of
// that, so the Go build fails with:
//
//     go: inconsistent vendoring in D:\MyProject\4Ceria:
//         github.com/go-chi/chi/v5@v5.5.0: is explicitly required in go.mod,
//         but not marked as explicit in vendor/modules.txt
//
// and the only escape is `-mod=mod` on every invocation — an environment
// variable that has to be set in CI, in the developer's shell, in the
// editor's Go tooling, and in every script that runs `go build`.
//
// A workspace file solves it, because the Go toolchain IGNORES a vendor
// directory in workspace mode. So the module stays at the repository root,
// `go build ./...` works from the root with no flags, and Composer's
// `vendor/` is left alone.
//
// The alternative — moving the Go module into a subdirectory — would also
// work, but it would put the Go code somewhere other than the root, and the
// root is where the plan, the CI jobs and the tools all expect it.
//
// `go.work` is checked in deliberately. It is not a local artefact: without
// it, `go build` at the root fails for every developer and in CI.

go 1.27.2

use .
